# core/what-depends-on-it - What depends on this element?
#
# Answers: concepts that depend on the focus, one or two steps out, along every
# predicate the attached vocabulary aligns with the core's dependency - a subproperty of
# depends_on, read from the concept that needs to the one needed, or of dependency_of,
# read the other way, as ArchiMate's serving and TOGAF's usedBy are (meta DD-44).
#
# Does NOT prove: that nothing else depends on the focus. Only what the model states
# is followed, along the predicates a metamodel aligns, two steps at most. A dependency
# recorded by an unaligned relationship type - an ArchiMate access, a C4 uses - is
# absent, and a modelled dependency is a statement, not an observed call.
#
# The template of the model question of the same name. `query run` asks the question
# where the dataset can be read as one graph; this answers elsewhere - an endpoint whose
# default graph is not the union of its graphs, or `query render` on named graphs.
#
# REQUIRES the vocabulary graph role. The alignment is declared in the published
# ontologies, and converter output carries none of them: attach them beside the data
# (examples/with-vocabulary). Without them this is refused, rather than answering from
# the core's two predicates alone, which reads as "nothing depends on it".
# core/dependents-direct follows predicates you name instead.
#
# Two steps, as the question goes. A predicate set read at query time cannot be
# followed to any depth: a SPARQL path takes no variable. Each step reads the predicates
# and the way each runs in the vocabulary, matches its triple both ways, and keeps the
# way the predicate reads. The second step has scopes of its own (vocabulary2,
# semantic2), because its predicate and its triple may sit in other graphs.
#
# Parameters: FOCUS_IRI, LIMIT
{{PREFIXES}}
SELECT DISTINCT ?hops ?dependent ?dependentLabel ?firstPredicate ?via ?secondPredicate
WHERE {
  {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:vocabulary}}
      { ?firstPredicate {{ROLE:subproperty_of}}* {{ROLE:depends_on}} . BIND(true AS ?firstNeeds) }
      UNION
      { ?firstPredicate {{ROLE:subproperty_of}}* {{ROLE:dependency_of}} . BIND(false AS ?firstNeeds) }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
      VALUES ?focus { {{FOCUS_IRI}} }
      { ?dependent ?firstPredicate ?focus . BIND(true AS ?firstRead) }
      UNION
      { ?focus ?firstPredicate ?dependent . BIND(false AS ?firstRead) }
      OPTIONAL { ?dependent {{PATH:label}} ?dependentLabel }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    FILTER(?firstRead = ?firstNeeds)
    BIND(1 AS ?hops)
  }
  UNION
  {
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:vocabulary}}
      { ?firstPredicate {{ROLE:subproperty_of}}* {{ROLE:depends_on}} . BIND(true AS ?firstNeeds) }
      UNION
      { ?firstPredicate {{ROLE:subproperty_of}}* {{ROLE:dependency_of}} . BIND(false AS ?firstNeeds) }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic}}
      VALUES ?focus { {{FOCUS_IRI}} }
      { ?via ?firstPredicate ?focus . BIND(true AS ?firstRead) }
      UNION
      { ?focus ?firstPredicate ?via . BIND(false AS ?firstRead) }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    FILTER(?firstRead = ?firstNeeds)
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:vocabulary2}}
      { ?secondPredicate {{ROLE:subproperty_of}}* {{ROLE:depends_on}} . BIND(true AS ?secondNeeds) }
      UNION
      { ?secondPredicate {{ROLE:subproperty_of}}* {{ROLE:dependency_of}} . BIND(false AS ?secondNeeds) }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    {{GRAPH_OPEN:semantic2}}
      { ?dependent ?secondPredicate ?via . BIND(true AS ?secondRead) }
      UNION
      { ?via ?secondPredicate ?dependent . BIND(false AS ?secondRead) }
      OPTIONAL { ?dependent {{PATH:label}} ?dependentLabel }
    {{GRAPH_CLOSE}}
    FILTER(?secondRead = ?secondNeeds)
    FILTER(?dependent != ?focus)
    BIND(2 AS ?hops)
  }
}
ORDER BY ?hops ?dependentLabel ?dependent
LIMIT {{LIMIT}}
